ip. Although still relatively unexplored, the manufacturing and styles of furniture differ by region. <br><br>This horseshoe-back armchair was made in Jiangsu province. Its simplicity and minimalist elegance is characteristic of Suzhou-style furniture and aesthetics. The back of the chair is made of seven pieces of wood, joined and secured with an inserted wooden pin, a mortise-tenon technique that appeared in its earliest form in Neolitihic fragments of the Hemudu culture.","did_you_know":"The horseshoe-shaped back of this chair is joined without glue or nails.","dimensions":{"overall":{"depth":0.584,"depth_inch":23,"depth_inch_fraction":0,"height":0.854,"height_inch":33,"height_inch_fraction":0.625,"length":0.636,"length_inch":25,"length_inch_fraction":0.0625}},"early_education_description":null,"edition_of_the_work":null,"exhibitions":{"current":[{"description":"<i>World Cultures and Modern Art: The Encounter of 19th and 20th Century European Art and Music with Asia, Africa, Oceania, Afro- and Indo-America</i>. Organisationskomitee fur die Spiele der XX. Olympiade, Munich, Germany (organizer) (May 15-September 30, 1972).","id":445204,"opening_date":"1972-05-15T04:00:00","title":"World Cultures and Modern Art: The Encounter of 19th and 20th Century European Art and Music with Asia, Africa, Oceania, Afro- and Indo-America"},{"description":"<i>Stories from Storage</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (organizer) (February 7-May 16, 2021).","id":383281,"opening_date":"2021-02-06T05:00:00","title":"Stories from Storage"},{"description":"<i>China’s Southern Paradise: Treasures from the Lower Yangzi Delta</i>. The Cleveland Museum of Art, Cleveland, OH (organizer) (September 10, 2023-January 7, 2024).","id":395234,"opening_date":"2023-09-10T04:00:00","title":"China’s Southern Paradise: Treasures from the Lower Yangzi Delta"}],"legacy":[]},"external_resources":{"internet_archive":["https://archive.org/details/clevelandart-1955.40.1-roundback-armchair-l"],"wiki